 ancestry resolves, and that same `has no parent` line under `--force` where the
 base is a root commit, since the existence check resolves NEWREF whatever
 `--force` says. Needs a branch whose tip holds a parent and a
 second branch holding one root commit, which the setup's single commit does not
 bind. The cited test also covers `-A` taking the same steps, and pins the
 tool's crash on the base the cell above states.

