family: M10
subcommand: checkout
cell: checkout/composefs-outside-the-backing-modes
modes: archive
setup: repo-with-commit
run: checkout --repo=$REPO --composefs $REV $SCRATCH/dest
expect-exit: 1
expect-stdout: empty
expect-stderr: contains "requires a bare-user or bare-user-shared repository"
ref-expect-exit: 0
ref-expect-stdout: empty
ref-expect-stderr: empty
outcome: lossy
severity: interop
loss: the composefs export from a repository outside the backing modes. The
 tool exports an image from any mode, and from an `archive` repository it writes
 `trusted.overlay.redirect` values naming `.file` loose paths that repository
 does not hold, so the image cannot be mounted against the repository that
 produced it. The port refuses the mode at exit 1, naming it: `error:
 unsupported: composefs export requires a bare-user or bare-user-shared
 repository, not Archive` (`cli-surface.md`, "P2").
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::checkout_composefs_refuses_an_archive_repository
spec: cli-surface.md#p2----options-missing-from-commands-that-exist
note: the two reach different exit statuses, so no oracle reads the pair. Both
 composefs switches carry the refusal. The cited test states it for each switch
 and holds the two facts an exit status does not: the refusal creates no
 destination, and it leaves a destination that already existed byte for byte and
 at the mode it carried.

