severity: interop
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::checkout_union_type_conflicts_match_the_tool
spec: format-reference.md#checkout
note: the conflicts no union mode resolves, each refused at exit 1 in both with
 the colliding entry untouched: an existing directory where the commit carries
 a regular file or a symlink, under `--union` and `--union-identical`; and an
 existing regular file where the commit carries a directory, under all three.
 `--union-add` is the one exception, keeping an existing directory where the
 commit carries a file and exiting 0. An existing symlink where the commit
 carries a directory is no conflict: all three modes follow it, so a link to a
 directory takes the subtree into the link's target at exit 0 and a dangling
 link is refused by the open the follow makes. The cited test states the
 destination each refusal leaves, which pins the write order: a directory's
 regular files and symlinks first in name order, then its subdirectories in
 name order.

