 against the tool's own destination.

family: M10
subcommand: checkout
cell: checkout/whiteouts-widen-a-union-type-conflict
setup: repo-with-commit
outcome: full
severity: interop
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::checkout_whiteouts_widen_a_union_type_conflict
spec: format-reference.md#checkout
note: `--whiteouts` widens the union-files disposition over a type conflict, for
 every entry and not only for a marker. Under `--union` with the switch a
 destination entry whose type is not the type the tree carries at that name is
 removed and the entry is written, at exit 0: a directory and its whole
 subtree, empty or populated, where the tree carries a regular file or a
 symlink, and a regular file, a symlink of any kind, a fifo, a device, or a
 socket where the tree carries a directory. A symlink loses the link alone, so
 the directory a link to a directory resolved to stays as it stands and
 receives nothing. The rule reaches the destination root and every depth below
 it, and the checkout mode, the repository mode, and `--subpath` make no
 difference. The destination directory a file subpath needs stands outside it,
 refusing a destination that is not a directory under either switch. The switch
 widens union-files alone: `--union-add` and `--union-identical` keep their own
 disposition, `--process-passthrough-whiteouts` widens nothing, and the
 whiteout device refuses a destination directory under either switch. The tree
 the cited test checks out holds no marker name, so the widening answers to the
 switch and not to a marker.

