evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::checkout_batch_ignores_subpath_and_takes_composefs
spec: format-reference.md#composefs
note: `--composefs` and `--composefs-noverity` are each taken alongside a batch
 option, and every pair writes the image of its own revision into the one
 destination, the pair's subpath deciding nothing. No oracle reads a cell's own
 checkout destination, so the cited test reads the image both implementations
 wrote and states the bytes equal.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# checkout -- the hardlink requirement, the directory-mode mask, and the
# uncompressed-object cache (Phase 17f).
#
# `-H/--require-hardlinks` refuses at the entry the checkout would materialize
# by a copy, so a cell that states a refusal names a corpus that reaches one and
# a cell that states an acceptance names one that does not. Corpus `C0` carries
# a regular file of non-zero length and a symlink, so it reaches every refusal;
# its directories and its empty file reach none. No oracle reads a cell's own
# checkout destination or the cache directory, so every destination claim and
# every link-count claim cites the test that walks both implementations'
# destinations. The words of each refusal part, which cli-surface.md,
# "checkout" records, so a refusal cell names `exit-status stdout-text` and
# states the tool's words with `ref-expect-stderr`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

