family: M10
subcommand: checkout
cell: checkout/require-hardlinks-refuses-at-the-entry
setup: repo-with-commit
outcome: full
severity: interop
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::checkout_require_hardlinks_refuses_at_the_entry,
 ostrya_cli::cli::checkout_require_hardlinks_and_skip_list_and_subpath_match_the_tool
spec: format-reference.md#checkout
note: `-H` decides per entry. A directory never refuses, a zero-length regular
 file never refuses, a regular file of non-zero length refuses wherever the
 repository mode and the checkout mode in force give a copy, and a symlink
 refuses in `archive` under either checkout mode and in `bare` under `-U`. A
 commit holding none of the refusing shapes is written whole at exit 0 in every
 mode. The first cited test states all thirty-two cells against the tool, one
 single-shape commit per cell; no single invocation can. The second states that
 a `--skip-list` pruning every refusing entry gives exit 0 and that a
 `--subpath` naming the empty file gives exit 0 where one naming the symlink
 gives exit 1, in both.

