 and under both checkout modes.

family: M10
subcommand: checkout
cell: checkout/require-hardlinks-across-devices
setup: repo-with-commit
outcome: refused-both
severity: interop
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::checkout_require_hardlinks_refuses_across_devices
spec: format-reference.md#checkout
note: a destination directory on another filesystem than the repository is
 refused before any entry of it is written, whatever the subtree holds, and both
 leave the destination directory created and empty. The check is repeated at
 every destination directory the walk enters, the destination root and every
 directory below it, fresh or reused; a directory below the root is reached by a
 destination symlink into a second filesystem, which a union mode follows. A
 `--subpath` naming a file or a symlink reaches no directory walk and takes no
 such check, so a zero-length regular file is written there at exit 0 and a
 shape the mode pair hardlinks is refused at the link. The harness binds one
 scratch subtree per side and cannot name a second filesystem, so the claim is
 stated by the cited test, which runs where one is reachable and states nothing
 where none is. The words part: the tool writes `Unable to do hardlink checkout
 across devices (src=<dev> destination=<dev>)` for a destination directory and
 `Hardlinking <object> to <name>: Invalid cross-device link` for a file or
 symlink target.

