# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# checkout -- durability (Phase 17f, F16).
#
# `--fsync=POLICY` carries the value set, the refusal text, and the narrowing
# rule the vocabulary states, and it changes no byte of the destination. No
# oracle reads a cell's own checkout destination, so the destination claim
# cites the test that walks both implementations' destinations, and the cells
# here run the acceptances and the refusals, which an exit status and a message
# state. The count of sync calls a policy produces is outside every oracle this
# harness reads, so it cites a test as well, and so does the reach of a
# configured `[core] fsync` value the reader refuses, which needs a repository
# config no setup here writes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

