family: M10
subcommand: show
cell: show/bad-signature-report
modes: archive
setup: repo-with-commit
outcome: lossy
severity: interop
loss: the instant and the algorithm name of the `Signature made` line, and the
 line under the verdict. The tool holds no instant and no algorithm for a
 signature the cryptography refused, so it draws the Unix epoch in the host
 locale and time zone (`Thu 01 Jan 1970 01:00:00 CET`) and `[unknown name]`,
 and the port draws an empty instant and `unknown`. The tool draws a
 `Primary key ID <key-id>` line under the verdict, which the port draws nowhere
 (`cli-surface.md`, "P1", states them all). The key id and the verdict line
 agree.
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::show_reports_a_bad_signature_like_the_tool
spec: format-reference.md#show
note: a signature the cryptography refuses needs a generated key, a remote
 keyring, and a stored signature that stands over another commit, which no
 setup binds. The cited test signs one commit with a key carrying a signing
 subkey, copies that commit's detached metadata onto another commit, and
 imports the public keyring into the remote the report reads. Both
 implementations name the signing subkey on the report line, by the trailing
 sixteen hex digits of its fingerprint, and both refuse the signature in the
 words `BAD signature from "<user id>"`. The same test states the three
 differences the outcome names, so a move in either implementation is reported.

