spec: format-reference.md#ls
note: a `..` component is an entry name that no directory of a commit tree
 holds, so the path names nothing and the listing is refused. A `PATH` names
 entries and does not climb out of the directory it stands in. `nested.txt`
 is a name `dir` holds, so a walk that drops the `..` reaches `dir/nested.txt`
 and lists it at exit 0. This cell fails such a walk. The port names the whole
 path, and the tool names the prefix that failed:
 `Inspecting path 'dir/../nested.txt': No such file or directory: /dir/..`.
 `stderr-text` is not an oracle here.

