 and the root holds none, which refuses the path the same way. `file.txt` is a
 name the commit root holds, so a walk that drops the `..` reaches `file.txt`
 and lists it at exit 0. This cell fails such a walk. The tool reports
 `No such file or directory: /..` after the quoted argument and the port names
 the whole path, so `stderr-text` is not an oracle here.

