note: corpus `C2` holds `04755`, `02755`, and `01755` as regular files and
 `02775` and `01777` as directories, so the checksum states the rule and the
 two limits on it at once: the write bits of an executable file go, setuid,
 setgid, and sticky survive, and a directory is left alone whatever its mode.
 Corpus `C1` would add the modes with no execute bit; it also holds a `0000`
 file, which neither implementation can read as a non-root user, so the forms
 cell below carries those instead.

