 `dir1((`, `\q`, and `(*BOGUS)f` part on the reason alone. The unit `N` counts
 is the other: the port reports the code-unit offset PCRE2 answers, the tool
 reports a character offset. The two agree over an expression that holds ASCII
 characters alone ahead of the error point, which is the five named above, and
 the cited test states each of the five lines. A non-ASCII character ahead of
 the error point parts the offsets by the code units that character occupies
 beyond the first: `\q` behind one `é` reports char 3 from the port and char 2
 from the tool, and behind one `U+1F600` char 5 and char 2. The cited test
 states both offsets over eight such expressions, so an assertion holds the
 divergence (`cli-surface.md`, "Scope of CLI compatibility"). Both need a
 `tar=` source, which no setup binds.

