setup: repo-with-commit
outcome: lossy
severity: interop
loss: the value dialect. The tool reads the whole value as a name to look up,
 so `/dir/` names nothing and the export ends at exit 1 with `No such file or
 directory: /dir/`. The port reads a path, where the trailing slash names the
 same directory as the form without it, so the export succeeds and writes the
 archive `--subpath=/dir` writes. This is the dialect `checkout --subpath`
 already parts on (`cli-surface.md`, "P2").
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::export_subpath_refusals_match_the_tool
spec: cli-surface.md#p2----options-missing-from-commands-that-exist
