expect-exit: 1
expect-stderr: contains "error: Invalid depth 0x1"
ref-expect-exit: 0
ref-expect-stderr: empty
outcome: lossy
severity: interop
loss: the depth dialect. The tool reads a leading sign and a leading run of
 decimal digits and drops the rest of the string, so `0x1` and `0=1` read as
 depth 0, `+1`, ` 1`, and `1 ` read as depth 1, and an overflowing value reads
 as a very large depth. The port reads a decimal integer with an optional
 leading `-` and refuses each of those five at exit 1, removing nothing
 (`cli-surface.md`, "P2").
