outcome: full
severity: interop
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::summary_reading_options_match_the_tool
spec: format-reference.md#summary
note: over one summary, `--raw` wins over `--view`, over
 `--list-metadata-keys`, and over `--print-metadata-key`; `--view` wins over
 `--list-metadata-keys` and over `--print-metadata-key`; and
 `--list-metadata-keys` wins over `--print-metadata-key`. The winner does not
 depend on the order the switches are written in, which the cited test states
 by giving each competing pair in both orders.

family: M10
subcommand: summary
cell: summary/positional-ignored
setup: repo-with-commit
outcome: lossy
severity: interop
loss: a positional argument. The tool takes none and accepts one, ignoring it
 and writing the report as if it were absent. The port reads a positional as a
 signing key identifier, a surface the tool states with `--sign=KEY-ID`, and
 signing precedes every reading option, so a word that is no key refuses at
 exit 1 (`cli-surface.md`, "summary").
evidence: ostrya_cli::cli::summary_argument_handling_parts_from_the_tool
spec: cli-surface.md#p2----options-missing-from-commands-that-exist
note: the two reach different exit statuses, so no oracle reads the pair. The
 cited test states that the port writes no report beside the positional and
 that the tool writes one.

family: M10
